1. Sets defaults: 3 attempts, 100ms base delay
2. Creates and immediately invokes an async IIFE (Immediately Invoked Function Expression)
3. Loops for the specified number of attempts
4. Tries to execute the function
5. If successful: returns the result immediately
6. If fails: stores the error, waits exponentially, then retries
7. If all attempts fail: throws the last error

